# The SHA-256 of each server tarball this version of the plugin installs,
# one line per platform, in sha256sum's format:
#
#   SHA256  reminisce-mcp-VERSION-OS-ARCH.tar.gz
#
# scripts/install-server checks the tarball it downloads against the line
# here for it. A release's tarballs are built after the release is tagged,
# so the release's own commit pins none: install-server then checks against
# the release's own .sha256 file, and says that this finds a damaged
# download, not a release whose files were replaced. Once the release is
# published, a second commit of the same version writes its four lines here
# (the pin commit), and a plugin installed from that commit checks against
# them, independently of the release. The next release is not cut until it
# has been made.
